-- Upgrade candidates spanning the current two raid tiers (Trial of the Crusader /
-- T9, and Icecrown Citadel + Ruby Sanctum / T10), plus the badge-purchasable,
-- non-Sanctified version of each tier-10 set piece. The goal is coverage - every
-- realistic upgrade path, not just the single best-in-slot item - so weaker/older
-- pieces are intentionally still listed; Scoring.lua ranks them all by actual
-- delta over your currently equipped item, so lower entries here simply won't
-- outscore something you already have equipped.
--
-- Item IDs are cross-checked against the bundled AtlasLoot_WrathoftheLichKing data
-- file (Interface/AddOns/AtlasLoot_WrathoftheLichKing/wrathofthelichking.lua) so
-- they're guaranteed to exist as real items on a 3.3.5a client; stats are NOT
-- hand-typed here - Scoring.lua fetches them live via TooltipScan so numbers always
-- match this exact server's itemization, including any Warmane-specific tuning.
--
-- Entries are NOT tagged per spec. Instead:
--   armorType = "Cloth"/"Leather"/"Mail"/"Plate" for armor slots (head, shoulder,
--     chest, wrist, hands, waist, legs, feet) - Eligibility.lua checks this live
--     against the character's class.
--   classes = { "WARLOCK", ... } for weapon slots (main hand/off hand/ranged),
--     since weapon proficiency doesn't reduce to a simple type check.
--   Neither field: neck/back/ring/trinket, which anyone can equip regardless of
--     class or armor type.
-- Whatever passes eligibility is then ranked by Scoring.lua's per-spec stat
-- weights, so adding a new class later is just adding its StatWeights entry -
-- no need to retag every item in this file.
JohnnysGearAdvisor.ItemDB = {}
